     4	
     5	---
     6	
     7	## Strategy Catalog
     8	
     9	### H001 — SA Score Filter Tightening
    10	- **Source**: Deep Lead Optimization (JACS 2024)
    11	- **Tech**: SA threshold 8.0→6.0, added max_rings=7, fused ring penalty 0.5→1.0, spiro 1.0→1.5, bridgehead 1.5→2.0
    12	- **When to use**: When generating too many unsynthesizable molecules
    13	- **Status**: ✅ VERIFIED
    14	
    15	### H002 — Docking-Guided Generation
    16	- **Source**: MOOSE-Chem (Yang et al., 2025) + Coscientist (Boiko et al., 2023)
    17	- **Tech**: Embed docking as fitness function in generation loop; batch_size=10, n_generations=3, top_k=5
    18	- **When to use**: Always (default on). Verified +0.4~0.8 kcal/mol improvement
    19	- **Status**: ✅ VERIFIED
    20	
    21	### H003 — Recursive Multi-Step Synthesis
    22	- **Source**: LARC (Baker et al., 2025)
    23	- **Tech**: max_depth=3 recursive retrosynthesis; continue breaking intermediates until simple
    24	- **When to use**: Always (default in plan_synthesis_v2)
    25	- **Status**: ✅ VERIFIED
    26	
    27	### H009 — Consensus Docking
    28	- **Source**: Coscientist (Boiko et al., 2023) — "performing experiments multiple times"
    29	- **Tech**: 3 independent docking runs with different seeds, median as consensus score
    30	- **When to use**: For final top-N ranking
    31	- **Status**: ✅ VERIFIED
    32	
    33	### H010 — Scaffold Hopping Mutation
    34	- **Source**: Deep Lead Optimization (JACS 2024)
    35	- **Tech**: BRICS decompose → identify core → replace with different scaffold → reattach side chains
    36	- **When to use**: ~20% probability in mutation; improves scaffold diversity
    37	- **Status**: ✅ VERIFIED
    38	
    39	### H011 — Diversity-Preserving Selection (MMD)
    40	- **Source**: MOOSE-Chem (Yang et al., 2025)
    41	- **Tech**: Greedy Maximum Minimal Distance selection with 0.7×BE + 0.3×diversity
    42	- **When to use**: During seed selection in docking guidance (top_k=5 BE + rest diversity)
    43	- **Status**: ✅ VERIFIED — Best BE improved +19.3%
    44	
    45	### H012 — Route Quality Scoring (Agent-as-a-Judge)
    46	- **Source**: LARC (Baker et al., 2025)
    47	- **Tech**: Multi-step route scoring: reactant count, complexity ratio, step count bonus
    48	- **When to use**: Composite ranking 0.8×BE + 0.2×route_quality
    49	- **Status**: ✅ VERIFIED
    50	
    51	### H013 — Crossover (Fragment Recombination)
    52	- **Source**: MOOSE-Chem (Yang et al., 2025) + MolLEO (Wang et al., 2024b)
    53	- **Tech**: Swap Murcko scaffolds between parent molecules, reattach side chains
    54	- **When to use**: 25% probability in combine strategy and offspring generation
    55	- **Status**: ✅ VERIFIED
    56	
    57	### H014 — Mass Balance Validation
    58	- **Source**: LARC (Baker et al., 2025)
    59	- **Tech**: Validate reactant/target heavy atom ratio 0.7–1.3; reject rules that only match partial fragments
    60	- **When to use**: Run during _run_retro_rule; eliminates false matches
    61	- **Status**: ✅ VERIFIED
    62	
    63	### H015 — Saturated N-Heterocycle Synthesis Rules
    64	- **Source**: LARC (Baker et al., 2025) + JACS 2024
    65	- **Tech**: Added THIQ, indoline, tetrahydroquinoline, saturated cyclic amine C-N cleavage, benzazepine rules
    66	- **When to use**: Always in RETRO_RULES
    67	- **Status**: ✅ VERIFIED — achieved 0/10 trivial routes
    68	
    69	### H016 — Diels-Alder Retro Rules
    70	- **Source**: JACS 2024 (cycloaddition as key synthetic strategy)
    71	- **Tech**: Cyclohexene→butadiene+dienophile, dihydropyran→oxa-diene+dienophile
    72	- **When to use**: Always in RETRO_RULES
    73	- **Status**: ✅ VERIFIED
    74	
    75	### H017 — Lactone/Epoxide/Pyrazole/sp3C-sp3C Rules
    76	- **Source**: LARC (Baker et al., 2025) + JACS 2024
    77	- **Tech**: Lactone hydrolysis, epoxide ring-opening, Knorr pyrazole, sp3 C-C Grignard retro, cyclic ether opening
    78	- **When to use**: Always in RETRO_RULES
    79	- **Status**: ✅ VERIFIED
    80	
    81	### H018 — BRICS Fragment Recombination (Fixed)
    82	- **Source**: JACS 2024 (BRICS) + MOOSE-Chem (Yang et al., 2025)
    83	- **Tech**: Replaced string concatenation with BRICSBuild; fragment pool from docked molecules
    84	- **When to use**: combine strategy
    85	- **Status**: ✅ VERIFIED — avg BE -8.609
    86	
    87	### H019 — Suzuki Byproduct Atom Balance
    88	- **Source**: LARC (Baker et al., 2025) — atom conservation
    89	- **Tech**: Added REACTION_BYPRODUCTS dict for Suzuki (B(OH)2+Br loss), Friedländer (2H2O loss)
    90	- **When to use**: In _add_byproducts_for_balance
    91	- **Status**: ❌ REJECTED — trivial ratio regressed (1/10)
    92	
    93	### H020 — Diaryl Amine / Indole / Benzofuran / Tetrazole / Isoxazole Rules
    94	- **Source**: LARC (Baker et al., 2025) + JACS 2024
    95	- **Tech**: Fischer indole, Rap-Stoermer benzofuran, tetrazole [3+2], isoxazole condensation
    96	- **When to use**: Always in RETRO_RULES
    97	- **Status**: ✅ VERIFIED
    98	
    99	### H022 — Expanded Scaffold Library (Bridge/Spiro/Fused Heterocycles)
   100	- **Source**: MOOSE-Chem (Yang et al., 2025) + JACS 2024
   101	- **Tech**: Added BCP, quinuclidine, tropane, spiro-piperidine, azaindole, imidazopyridine scaffolds
   102	- **When to use**: Always in SCAFFOLDS
   103	- **Status**: ✅ VERIFIED
   104	
   105	### H025 — Expanded Substituent Library (Polar Pharmacophores)
   106	- **Source**: Deep Lead Optimization (JACS 2024) + Coscientist (2023)
   107	- **Tech**: Added 5 polar substituents (C=O, CN, CH2OH, CH2NH2, SO2CH3) to _add_substituent
   108	- **When to use**: When molecules lack hydrogen bond features
   109	- **Status**: ❌ REJECTED — Best BE -9.153→-8.972, Avg -8.453→-8.325. Vina scoring favors hydrophobic/flat aromatics over polar hinge binders.
   110	
   111	### H027 — Relaxed Molecular Filters
   112	- **Source**: Empirical (Round 18-19) — Vina rewards hydrophobic packing
   113	- **Tech**: max_rings 7→9, max_sa 6.0→7.0 in passes_filters(); allows larger hydrophobic aromatics
   114	- **When to use**: When current filters exclude >7-ring molecules that could pack better in Vina
   115	- **Status**: ✅ VERIFIED — Best BE +2.0% (-9.153→-9.332), Avg +4.2% (-8.453→-8.810)
   116	
   117	### H026 — Expanded Large Aromatic Scaffold Library
   118	- **Source**: JACS 2024 — scaffold diversity + Vina hydrophobic bias
   119	- **Tech**: Added 12 large polycyclic aromatic scaffolds (anthracene, phenanthrene, pyrene, perylene, acridine, benzoquinolines, benzo[a]pyrene)
   120	- **When to use**: N/A
   121	- **Status**: ❌ REJECTED — Best BE -9.332→-8.389, Avg -8.810→-7.989
   122	
   123	### H028 — Suzuki SMARTS Specificity Fix
   124	- **Source**: Empirical (Round 4 debugging) — discovered Suzuki [c;R][c;R] falsely matching fused ring C-C bonds
   125	- **Tech**: Changed SMARTS from [c;R][c;R] to [c;R]!@[c;R] to only match inter-ring (biaryl) bonds, not intra-ring fused bonds
   126	- **When to use**: Always in RETRO_RULES
   127	- **Status**: ✅ VERIFIED — Trivial ratio restored 1/10→0/10, BE -9.19 within baseline variance
